        "data": {
          "text": "Rank Collapse \u00b7 structured orthogonal scale-up of the Figure-5 mechanism.\nPhenomenon: this graph makes warmup \u2192 entropy expansion \u2192 terminal compression much larger and stable inside a disclosed local initialization neighborhood. It is a mechanism-focused stress test, not a second claim of exact Figure-5 numerical recovery.\nPaper setting: Figure 5 uses six orthogonal samples, labels [0,0,1,1,2,3], four classes, d=2, full-batch cross entropy and 300 plotted updates. The paper does not publish its learning rate, numerical initialization, seed or toy source.\nTemplate setting: the complete training set is X=I60 with grouped class counts [32,16,8,4], a bias-free linear 60\u21922\u21924 factorization, full-batch SGD(lr=0.06), and 400 updates. The balanced singular values are [0.90,0.50]. The robust_v1 functional input/head bases are label-aware: they are constructed from the grouped class partition, class mass and log-frequency contrasts. The evidence-locked input rotation angle/plane is 3.0 rad / 1 and the output rotation angle/plane is 1.7 rad / 2; these were selected by the disclosed search, not supplied by the paper. Gaussian perturbations use coefficient 0.05 before canonical QR (not a hard 5% radius); initialization still satisfies F\u1d40F=WW\u1d40.\nResult boundary: scripts/phenomena/rank_collapse_scaleup.py runs the canonical graph, all 200 disclosed perturbation seeds (0\u2013199), a global-random orientation robustness probe, uniform-frequency / d=3 no-bottleneck / MSE controls, plus longer horizons. Robustness means the neighborhood around this structured basis, not arbitrary random initialization. The late decline is finite-window and later re-expands, so persistent/asymptotic collapse is not claimed. This Template validates the Panel-D-style RankMe/spectrum signature, not the paper's classwise primacy ordering or complete Figure-5 B/C trajectories. CI only performs an in-memory short smoke and does not assert the phenomenon. No Grokking task is used.",
          "instanceTitle": "Structured scale-up \u00b7 claim boundary"
        }
      },
